d_or_disinfected\" with notComminutedOrDisinfected=false, and its SPARQL check only rejects the true combination rather than enforcing selector/boolean consistency. Make the selector the applicability driver and require the boolean to be true whenever that selector value is present; do not let the false branch bypass the conditional obligations. Remove the globally mandatory nearbyIceConcentration constraint, since it is conditional input. In the applicable case, retain ship-owned canonical QuantityValue structures and units, require MARPOL compliance true and distanceToNearestIceShelfOrFastIce > 12 MI_N, and encode that the recorded distanceFromAreaWithIceConcentrationAboveOneTenth is specifically associated with an area whose declared ice-concentration operand (the supplied nearbyIceConcentration) exceeds 0.1, rather than checking only presence of the distance result. Preserve the required ship-owned iceConcentration QuantityValue with UNITLESS units and all declared direct terms; do not introduce a new vocabulary term."],"current_feedback":"Reject: the SPARQL constraint is an accidental pass/violation inversion. It SELECTs a ship only when the applicable discharge type, true boolean, true MARPOL status, distance >12 MI_N, nearby ice concentration >0.1, and area-distance record are all present; in SHACL-SPARQL this makes compliant data fail while missing or false obligations can pass. Rewrite it as a violation query for the implication: when sewageDischargeType is \"not_comminuted_or_disinfected\", require notComminutedOrDisinfected=true, MARPOL compliance=true, distanceToNearestIceShelfOrFastIce with unit MI_N and numericValue >12, nearbyIceConcentration with unit UNITLESS and numericValue >0.1, and a ship-owned distanceFromAreaWithIceConcentrationAboveOneTenth record with unit MI_N. Encode missing, wrong-unit, false, and threshold-failing alternatives as violation branches (for example UNION branches), without OPTIONAL nested inside FILTER NOT EXISTS. Preserve the supplied ship target, canonical QuantityValue structures and units, required ship-owned iceConcentration with UNITLESS, strict >12 comparison, and the conditional association between the recorded area distance and the nearby concentration exceeding 0.1; do not introduce a new vocabulary term or make conditional properties globally mandatory.","blocking":false,"semantic_attempt_consumed":false}
